<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tughlugh Timur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1312–<a href="/years/1363">1363</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Tughlugh Timur Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tughlugh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>, the eastern part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a>, from 1347 to 1363. Raised to the throne by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dughlat">Dughlat</a> amir Puladchi, he converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> around 1354, reportedly with many of his followers. He invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> in 1360 and 1361, installing his son Ilyas Khoja there, and the young Timur first rose to prominence in his service.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tughlugh-timur.jpg" alt="Tughlugh Timur" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N. N. Pantusov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tughlugh_Timur_Mausoleum_-_exterior.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
